---
title: "pg_dump_export (Daily DB Backup Workflow)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_read_env: DATABASE_URL = secrets.SUPABASE_DB_URL
    q_read_env --> q_validate_url: DATABASE_URL is set
    q_read_env --> q_error: DATABASE_URL is empty
    q_validate_url --> q_dump: pg_dump invocation
    q_dump --> q_write: pg_dump DATABASE_URL --format=custom --no-owner --no-privileges -f backup.dump
    q_write --> [*]: backup.dump written to disk
    q_error --> [*]: step fails, DATABASE_URL missing

    note right of q_read_env
        INV-001: DATABASE_URL sourced from secrets.SUPABASE_DB_URL, never hardcoded
        INV-002: --no-owner and --no-privileges ensure portable dump without role dependencies
    end note

    note right of q_dump
        INV-003: --format=custom produces compressed binary dump suitable for pg_restore
        INV-004: output file backup.dump is written to runner workspace root
    end note
